    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i guess it's a bit of both. but it feels like the \"interdependence\" argument is used a lot to justify policies that actually hurt working class people in developed nations, like outsourcing everything to the cheapest possible place. if a country can't even make its own basic goods anymore because of these globalist frameworks, isn't that inherently unstable regardless of what the trade stats say?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
