      "content": "You are pointing to the critical difference between theoretical efficiency and practical resilience in highly globalized systems. Extreme dependency on single, distant sources introduces tremendous fragility, as demonstrated by recent pandemics and geopolitical tensions. Therefore, prioritizing diversification and domestic capacity over absolute lowest-cost sourcing can be seen as a pragmatic adaptation toward greater, though perhaps less efficient, human security.",
      "source": "target",
